# Text files are checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# `cargo fmt --check` runs on all three CI hosts, and rustfmt's
# default `newline_style = "Auto"` writes the *native* line ending.
# Without this, a file committed with CRLF passes the Windows job and
# fails the Linux one -- the gate would depend on which machine ran
# it. rustfmt.toml pins the same thing on the Rust side.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mkv binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.xz binary
